{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.ToffoliLpStability","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.ToffoliLpStability","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","lean:module:QOU.GroundRingCore","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt"],"declarations":65,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.ocneanu_numerator_vanishes_at_content_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.ocneanu_numerator_vanishes_at_content_neg","kind":"theorem","line":924,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L924-L943","doc":"**The row bound, formally.**  At a cell of content `-N`, the Ocneanu\nnumerator vanishes identically whenever the framing ratio is `q^N`.\n\nSince a partition with more than `N` rows always contains such a cell, this\nis why `w_λ = 0` there — and at `N = 2` it is why the corpus's exact\n`y_(1³) = 0` holds.  It is also what refutes the Wenzl-bridge premise\n`y_λ = w̃_λ` on the `κ_λ = 0` stratum: at `(3,1,1)` and `(3,2,1)` the left\nside is `0` by this lemma while `w̃_λ` is a ratio of positive quantum\nintegers, so the identity asserts `0 = positive` and no parameter can\nreconcile it\n(`computations/probes/wenzl_bridge_self_conjugate_premise_is_false.py`,\n10/10). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.ocneanu_numerator_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.ocneanu_numerator_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":912,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L912-L922","doc":"**The Ocneanu numerator collapses at framing `a = q^N`.**  Stated at the\ncell content `c` as a natural-number offset, which is all the `n = 3`\nweights below need: `z q^c - z₋ q^{-c} = z₋ q^N (q^{N+c} - q^{-(N+c)})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.markovZAt_two_eq_markovZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.markovZAt_two_eq_markovZ","kind":"theorem","line":890,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L890-L910","doc":"**Convention D is the `N = 2` member.**  `z₂ = q⁴ħ/(q⁴-1) = q³/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.markovZAt_framing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.markovZAt_framing","kind":"theorem","line":881,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L881-L888","doc":"**The defining property of the family: the framing ratio is `q^{2N}`.**\n`z_N = q^{2N}·(z_N - ħ)`, for every `N` — this is what makes the Ocneanu\nnumerator collapse into quantum integers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.markovZAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.markovZAt","kind":"def","line":876,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L876-L879","doc":"The Ocneanu family member with framing ratio `a = q^N`, in the form\n`z_N = q^{2N}ħ/(q^{2N} - 1)`; equivalently `q^N/[N]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qIntSym_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qIntSym_two","kind":"theorem","line":854,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L854-L874","doc":"`[2]_q` agrees with the quantum dimension `q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qIntSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qIntSym","kind":"def","line":851,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L851-L852","doc":"The symmetric quantum integer `[m]_q = (q^m - q^{-m})/(q - q^{-1})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.markovZ_eq_qsq_div_qDimTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.markovZ_eq_qsq_div_qDimTwo","kind":"theorem","line":800,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L800-L808","doc":"**`z = q²/[2]_q` in convention D** — the exact analogue of the form\n`z = 1/[2]_{√q}` that `prop:markov-z-reconciliation` already gives for\nconvention C, which makes the two conventions comparable at a glance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.markov_framing_ratio_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.markov_framing_ratio_eq","kind":"theorem","line":787,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L787-L798","doc":"**The Ocneanu framing ratio is a monomial in convention D**: `a² = q⁴`,\nso `a = q²`.  This is a *structural* reason for the convention-D ruling,\nindependent of the empirical one on record (195.8 ppm on `tr_M(β_Bor)`) —\nno anchor and no measurement enters.  Convention C's framing ratio is\n`-q^{3/2}/(-q^{3/2} + q³ + q² - q - 1)`, not a monomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.markov_loop_value_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.markov_loop_value_product","kind":"theorem","line":773,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L773-L785","doc":"**The two crossing loop values multiply to `1/[2]_q²`** (convention D).\n\nEquivalently `[2]_q² · z₊ · z₋ = 1`, which is `markov_hecke_relation` in\nclosed form.  Convention C satisfies no such identity: there `z₊z₋` has\nhalf-integer and integer powers of `q` mixed in one numerator and does not\nfactor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.markovZNeg_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.markovZNeg_eq","kind":"theorem","line":763,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L763-L771","doc":"`z₋ = 1/(q(q²+1))` in convention D — the negative-crossing loop value in\nclosed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qDimTwo_sq_sub_hbar_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qDimTwo_sq_sub_hbar_sq","kind":"theorem","line":754,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L754-L761","doc":"`[2]_q² - ħ² = 4` — the quantum dimension and the Hecke deformation are a\nhyperbolic pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.markovZNeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.markovZNeg","kind":"def","line":750,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L750-L752","doc":"The negative-crossing loop value `z₋ = z - ħ`, forced by the Hecke\nquadratic relation (`prop:markov-z-reconciliation`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qDimTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qDimTwo","kind":"def","line":747,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L747-L748","doc":"The quantum dimension `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.markov_hecke_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.markov_hecke_relation","kind":"theorem","line":705,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L705-L729","doc":"**The Markov parameter and the Hecke deformation are algebraically\ndependent**, satisfying the degree-4 irreducible relation\n\n`ħ³z - ħ²z² + 4ħz - 4z² + 1 = 0`.\n\nConsequence, and the reason it is stated here: `ℚ[z, ħ]` is *not* a\npolynomial ring but the coordinate ring of an affine rational curve, so a\npolynomial representative of any element is unique only modulo this\nrelation.  In particular the coefficient string of\n`cone_eq_markov_hecke_polynomial` carries no information — the degree-6\nrepresentatives of that one constraint form a six-parameter family.  What\n*is* invariant is the minimal degree.\n\nThis is a fact about `H_n(q)` and its Markov trace, not about the\n`q`-Toffoli. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.cone_eq_markov_hecke_polynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.cone_eq_markov_hecke_polynomial","kind":"theorem","line":671,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L671-L703","doc":"**The cone constraint is a degree-6 integer polynomial in `(z, ħ)`.**\n\n`(G·t)₅ = z² + 2ħz + 3ħ²z² + ħ³z + ħ⁴z²`\n\nCoefficients `(1, 2, 3, 1, 1)`; no denominators.  **Degree 6 is minimal** —\nno polynomial in `(z, ħ)` of total degree ≤ 5 equals it — and minimal degree\nis a genuine invariant of the class.\n\n⚠ **The coefficient string is NOT an invariant.**  `z` and `ħ` are\nalgebraically dependent (`markov_hecke_relation` below), so a representative\nis unique only modulo that relation; the degree-6 representatives form a\nsix-parameter family, and `-1 + 4z² - 3ħz + 4z⁴ + ħ²z⁴` is an equally\nintegral one.  Do not read meaning into `(1, 2, 3, 1, 1)`.  A reproducible\nchoice is the grevlex normal form modulo the relation,\n`ħ⁵z + 4ħ³z + ħ² - 2ħz + 5z² - 1`, and even that depends on the term order.\n(`computations/probes/toffoli_cone_in_markov_hecke_parameters.py`, 18/18.)\n\nBoth parameters are needed: the minimal polynomial of the constraint over\n`ℚ(z)` has degree 3 and over `ℚ(ħ)` degree 2, so it is a function of\nneither alone.  `ℚ(z, ħ) = ℚ(q)` — those degrees are coprime — so the\ncontent here is the *subring* statement, not a field statement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliDiagonal_eq_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliDiagonal_eq_markov","kind":"theorem","line":660,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L660-L669","doc":"**`tr(σ₀σ₁σ₀) = ħz² + z`.**  Not a finding of this arc — the value is\nalready tabulated at `QOU.Machinery.MarkovTraceH4.TRM` entries 9 and 13.\nRecorded here in the form the constraint below consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.markovZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.markovZ","kind":"def","line":656,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L656-L658","doc":"The Markov parameter, convention D (`z = q³/(q²+1)`).  The bare name\n`markovZ` denotes convention D uniformly across the corpus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.cone_eq_quadratic_in_amplitudes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.cone_eq_quadratic_in_amplitudes","kind":"theorem","line":601,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L601-L633","doc":"**The cone condition is a degree-2 polynomial in four of the amplitudes.**\n\nAn exact identity over `ℚ(q)`, valid for every `q > 0`:\n\n`(G·t)₅ = -4/9 + 5/36·M₀₀² - 20/3·M₀₀M₃₃ - 10/9·M₀₀M₄₄ + 5/18·M₀₀P₇₇`\n`        - 28/9·M₃₃² + 20/3·M₃₃M₄₄ + 38/9·M₃₃P₇₇ + 20/9·M₄₄² + 5/36·P₇₇²`\n\nOnly `+` and `×` appear on the right: no division by an amplitude, hence no\nreconstruction of `q`.  Note the *cross* terms — the identity is false\nwithout them (the span of `{1}` together with the amplitudes and their\nsquares alone does not contain the cone coordinate).\n\nThis is *a* solution, not *the* solution: the solution space carries one\nfree parameter over this four-amplitude span.  Whether any member has a\nHecke-theoretic reading is open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.coneCoordRow5_pos_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.coneCoordRow5_pos_iff","kind":"theorem","line":592,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L592-L599","doc":"**The cone coordinate's sign is its numerator's.**  The denominator\n`(q²+1)²` is strictly positive, so every threshold statement proved about\n`coneRow5Numerator` transfers verbatim to the constraint itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.coneCoordRow5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.coneCoordRow5","kind":"def","line":586,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L586-L590","doc":"The LP cone coordinate itself — row 5 of `G·t`, indexed by the longest\nHecke normal-form word `σ₀σ₁σ₀`.  This is the single constraint of the six\nthat changes sign; `coneRow5Numerator` is its numerator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliM44","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliM44","kind":"def","line":583,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L583-L584","doc":"The convention-D diagonal `M₄₄ = (q²+1)/(4q³)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliM33","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliM33","kind":"def","line":580,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L580-L581","doc":"The convention-D diagonal `M₃₃ = q(q²+1)/4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliM00","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliM00","kind":"def","line":577,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L577-L578","doc":"The convention-D diagonal `M₀₀ = (q⁴+1)/(q³(q²+1)²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.cone_sign_change_unexplained_by_factors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.cone_sign_change_unexplained_by_factors","kind":"theorem","line":535,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L535-L550","doc":"**The reduction is refuted, without appeal to signs or precision.**  Across\n`[1/2, 9/10]` the cone constraint changes sign, while `P₇₇·W_std` and `P₇₆`\nare both strictly positive at each endpoint.  No product of factors that do\nnot change sign can change sign, so the cone condition is not\n`P₇₇·W_std` modulated by anything depending only on `P₇₆`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.coneRow5Numerator_nineTenths_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.coneRow5Numerator_nineTenths_pos","kind":"theorem","line":531,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L531-L533","doc":"The cone constraint is already positive at `q = 9/10`, below `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.cone_threshold_ne_amplitude_threshold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.cone_threshold_ne_amplitude_threshold","kind":"theorem","line":495,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L495-L505","doc":"**The cone threshold is strictly below the amplitude's.**  At `q = 1` the\nflip amplitude vanishes while the cone constraint is strictly positive, so\nthe two do not change sign at the same place.  This refutes the negative-\nproportionality reduction, which would require them to coincide; together\nwith `toffoliFlip_mul_coneCoord_nonpos` (which excludes the sign-inheriting\nform) the proof's reduction has no surviving form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.coneRow5Numerator_half_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.coneRow5Numerator_half_neg","kind":"theorem","line":491,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L491-L493","doc":"The constraint is violated at `q = 1/2`, so a threshold exists below `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.coneRow5Numerator_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.coneRow5Numerator_one","kind":"theorem","line":486,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L486-L489","doc":"**The cone constraint is strictly satisfied at the classical limit.**\n`(G·t)₅`'s numerator equals `1` at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.coneRow5Poly_strictMono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.coneRow5Poly_strictMono","kind":"theorem","line":463,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L463-L484","doc":"`coneRow5Poly` is strictly increasing on `u ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.quad_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.quad_pos","kind":"theorem","line":460,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L460-L461","doc":"`3u² - 2u + 1 > 0` for every real `u` — negative discriminant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.coneRow5Numerator_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.coneRow5Numerator_eq","kind":"theorem","line":455,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L455-L458","doc":"The substitution `u = q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.coneRow5Numerator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.coneRow5Numerator","kind":"def","line":451,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L451-L453","doc":"The numerator of `(G·t)₅`, the one constraint that governs the cone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.coneRow5Poly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.coneRow5Poly","kind":"def","line":448,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L448-L449","doc":"The cone constraint's numerator after the substitution `u = q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.tracedVolume_product_eq_trace_of_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.tracedVolume_product_eq_trace_of_markov","kind":"theorem","line":405,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L405-L418","doc":"**The traced-volume factorisation is the Markov property.**  Given only\n`tr(1) = 1` and the Markov rule `tr(x·σ_last) = z·tr(x)`, the trace of the\nchain product equals the product of the traced volumes.  Stated with the\ntrace values as hypotheses, so it is a theorem about the Markov property\nrather than about any particular convention or anchor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliDiagonal_mul_wStd_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliDiagonal_mul_wStd_pos","kind":"theorem","line":377,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L377-L382","doc":"**The surviving half of the LP reduction.** `P₇₇ · W_std > 0` on `q > 0`,\nso the first factor of the proof's reduction never obstructs feasibility;\neverything at issue sits in the off-diagonal sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.wStd_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.wStd_pos","kind":"theorem","line":373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L373-L375","doc":"**`W_std > 0`** for every `q > 0`: the denominator has no real root. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoli_not_antisymmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoli_not_antisymmetric","kind":"theorem","line":358,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L358-L371","doc":"**The flip channel is not antisymmetric.** `P₆₇ ≠ -P₇₆` for every `q > 0`\nother than the classical limit, so \"reversing the crossing negates it\" is\nfalse — and it fails in convention C and D alike. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoli_antisymmetry_defect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoli_antisymmetry_defect","kind":"theorem","line":348,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L348-L356","doc":"**The antisymmetry defect, exactly.** `P₆₇ + P₇₆ = q(q-1)²(q+1)²/(2(q²+1))`,\nwhich is `0` only at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliFlip_pos_of_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliFlip_pos_of_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L333-L346","doc":"**`P₇₆ > 0` on `0 < q < 1`.** The sign structure is the mirror of the\namplitude's, which is what makes the excised convention's regime wrong. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliFlip_neg_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliFlip_neg_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L323-L331","doc":"**`P₇₆ < 0` on `q > 1`** — including the substrate anchor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliFlip_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliFlip_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L309-L321","doc":"**The only positive zero of `P₇₆` is `q = 1`** — the classical limit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliConeCoord_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliConeCoord_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L300-L307","doc":"`ħ = 0` exactly at `q = 1`, on `q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliConeCoord_pos_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliConeCoord_pos_iff","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L280-L298","doc":"The cone coordinate `ħ = q - q⁻¹` is positive exactly above `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliP66_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliP66_pos","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L276-L278","doc":"**`P₆₆` is strictly positive** for every `q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliDiagonal_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliDiagonal_pos","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L271-L274","doc":"**`P₇₇` has no positive root.** Strictly positive for every `q > 0`, so the\ngolden-ratio threshold `q⋆` of the excised convention C has no analogue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.wStd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.wStd","kind":"def","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L268-L269","doc":"The Wedderburn weight of the 2-dimensional standard representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliReverseFlip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliReverseFlip","kind":"def","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L264-L266","doc":"The convention-D reverse-flip amplitude `P₆₇`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliP66","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliP66","kind":"def","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L260-L262","doc":"The convention-D even-channel diagonal `P₆₆`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliDiagonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliDiagonal","kind":"def","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L256-L258","doc":"The convention-D diagonal `P₇₇ = q³(q⁴+1)/(q²+1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliFlip_mul_coneCoord_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliFlip_mul_coneCoord_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L222-L233","doc":"**Opposite signs, identically.** On `q > 0` the flip amplitude and the LP\ncone coordinate never share a sign: their product is non-positive.  This is\nthe invariant that excludes a sign-inheriting reduction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliFlipAmplitude_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliFlipAmplitude_eq","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L213-L220","doc":"**The factorisation.** `P₇₆ = -ħ · S / (2(q²+1)²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliSextic_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliSextic_pos","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L208-L211","doc":"`S(q) > 0` for every real `q`: every exponent is even, every coefficient\npositive, and the constant term is `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliConeCoord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliConeCoord","kind":"def","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L205-L206","doc":"The NF coordinate of `T_q` on the word `(0,1)`, namely `ħ = q - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliFlipAmplitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliFlipAmplitude","kind":"def","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L201-L203","doc":"The derived convention-D target-flip amplitude `P₇₆`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoliSextic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoliSextic","kind":"def","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L198-L199","doc":"The sextic cofactor `S(q) = q⁶ + q⁴ + 2q² + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoli_lp_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoli_lp_stable","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L114-L152","doc":"**The golden-ratio threshold of `f(q) = q + √q - 1`.**\n`f` is positive exactly above q⋆ = (3 - √5) / 2 = 1 / φ².\n\nSCOPE (2026-08-30): this is a statement about the real function `f`\nand nothing else.  `f` is the numerator of the **convention-C**\nToffoli diagonal, which is excised; the canonical convention-D\ndiagonal `q³(q⁴+1)/(q²+1)²` is positive for every `q > 0` and has\nno threshold.  So this theorem no longer establishes LP-stability\nof the q-Toffoli, and must not be cited for it — see the file\nheader.  The proof below is unchanged and remains correct.\nLabel: prop:toffoli-lp-stability\nRef: [leitner2026] Chapter 8, prop:toffoli-transfer-matrix\nRef: [leitner2026] Chapter 4, prop:lp-dual-stability ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:toffoli-lp-stability","label":"prop:toffoli-lp-stability","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.f_strict_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.f_strict_mono","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L107-L112","doc":"**Monotonicity of `f(q) = q + √q - 1` on `[0, ∞)`.** Strict. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.f_at_q_star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.f_at_q_star","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L100-L105","doc":"**Value at the threshold**: `q⋆ + √q⋆ - 1 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.sqrt_q_star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.sqrt_q_star","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L84-L98","doc":"`√q⋆ = (√5 - 1) / 2`.  Equivalently, `q⋆ = ((√5 - 1)/2)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.q_star_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.q_star_pos","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L74-L82","doc":"`0 < q⋆`: the golden-ratio threshold is strictly positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.q_star_golden_square","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.q_star_golden_square","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L65-L72","doc":"**Golden-ratio threshold identity.** `q⋆ · φ² = 1`.\nClosed-form identity underpinning `prop:toffoli-lp-stability`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.q_star_threshold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.q_star_threshold","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L62-L63","doc":"The golden-ratio threshold `q⋆ = (3 - √5) / 2 = 1 / φ²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.phi_golden","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.phi_golden","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L59-L60","doc":"The golden ratio `φ = (1 + √5) / 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.toffoli_diag_numerator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.toffoli_diag_numerator","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/toffoli-lp-stability.lean#L50-L57","doc":"The Toffoli diagonal numerator in the base ring `R_q`, under the\ncanonical convention D: `P₇₇(q) = q³(q⁴+1)/(q²+1)²` has numerator\n`q³(q⁴+1) = q⁷ + q³`.  This is exact, not a stub — the convention-D\ndiagonal is a Laurent polynomial over a positive denominator, so\nunlike its convention-C predecessor `q + q^(1/2) - 1` it needs no\nsquare-root extension of `R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}